# Working in AppBuilderSdk / AppBuilderShared

## Repository layout

- **Two git repos.** Root `AppBuilderSdk` (usually `development`) contains `src/shared`, a separate clone of `AppBuilderShared`. Shared changes: `git -C src/shared ...`. Root only records the shared pointer ("shared update") plus app, tests, and `public/`.
- **New worktrees:** follow `.cursor/rules/worktree-shared-repo.mdc` (proactively ensure `.vscode/settings.json` exists with `git.scanRepositories: ["src/shared"]`, run `git submodule init` & `update`, and checkout task branch in both repos).
- **Path alias:** `@AppBuilderLib/...` → `src/shared/...`. FSD: `entities/` (parameter, session, viewport), `features/`, `widgets/`, `shared/`. Tests live in `__tests__` next to the module (`jsdom` env header for store tests).
- **App Builder actions:** one `{ isAction, component?, run? }` table. Shared headless `run`s live in `features/appbuilder/model/appBuilderActionCatalog.ts` (no UI imports). `features/appbuilder/ui/sharedAppBuilderActions.ts` spreads those runs and adds shared **components** (including `executeActions`). `AppBuilderActionFromType` and `runAppBuilderAction` both overlay `componentContext.actions` by key (host match first; a host key with no `component` / no `run` does **not** fall through). Toolbar components may still call typed `runAppBuilderAction*.ts` helpers on click. There are no `useAppBuilderAction*` hooks. Do **not** put `ar` / `camera` / `fullscreen` in that shared table — that would import viewer UI into every host. ShapeDiver registers them from `src/AppBuilderRoot.tsx`. iJewel omits the key (no button, sequence warns), registers `{ isAction }` to suppress both, or supplies a native `component` + `run` (e.g. WebGi). Matching host entry with no `run` skips in sequences (no ShapeDiver fallback). Nested `executeActions` is allowed (`runAppBuilderActions` special-cases it to avoid a circular catalog import). Sequential mode awaits each action and then `waitForAppBuilderSessionIdle()`; `setParameterValues` awaits source resolution (`resolveParameterValueSources`) and `batchParameterValueUpdate`. An `agentTool` value source cannot be resolved in executeActions and fails the sequence. Undo/redo restore parameter history via `restoreHistoryStateFromIndex` (awaited) instead of `window.history.back()`, so they cannot navigate away from the app. Camera `zoomTo` `nameFilter` in the ShapeDiver `run` gathers current output/instance nodes via `findNodesByNameFilter` at each trigger. Import-parameter file pickers and import-model-state dialogs open from the `run` and wait for the user. Host-registered AR opens native `viewInAR` or the QR modal. Host-registered fullscreen `run` cycles `fullscreen3States` via `cycleFullscreen3States` (same DOM + `viewerFullscreen3States` store as the toolbar button).
- **Action slots (SS-10028):** Node-level `actionSlots` call the same `runAppBuilderAction` catalog (including nested `executeActions`). AR QR modal and import-model-state dialog stay mounted on `AppBuilderPage`. UI wrapper: `features/appbuilder/ui/AppBuilderActionSlots.tsx` (pointer/`click` only — no viewer viewport import). Application listeners: `features/appbuilder/ui/AppBuilderApplicationActionSlots.tsx`. Scene select/hover is **host-registered** like `ar` / `camera` / `fullscreen` / `waitUntilReady`: `IComponentContext.interactionSlotListeners` (props type `AppBuilderInteractionSlotListenersProps` in `ComponentContext.types.ts`). ShapeDiver registers `{ component: AppBuilderInteractionSlotListeners }` from `src/AppBuilderRoot.tsx` (`useSelection` + `viewer.viewport`). iJewel omits the key (warns when JSON has `selecton` / `selectoff` / `hoveron` / `hoveroff`), registers `{ }` to suppress both, or supplies a native `component` that calls `handlersRef` via `actionSlotHandlerKey`. A host entry with no `component` does **not** fall through to ShapeDiver. Do **not** import `AppBuilderInteractionSlotListeners` from shared application-slot wiring. **Allowlists** live in `APP_BUILDER_SLOT_EVENTS` (`features/appbuilder/lib/appBuilderActionSlots.ts`): widget/tab/container/control/toolbar/viewport currently all alias `APP_BUILDER_UI_EVENTS`; `application` is `APP_BUILDER_APPLICATION_EVENTS`; ignored names on the root are logged against `root` (union of application + UI). Call sites pass `allowedEvents={APP_BUILDER_SLOT_EVENTS.<kind>}`. Zod does not restrict which events a node may use. A slot value may be one object or an **array** of objects (same event, different `eventProps` — e.g. several root `selecton` nameFilters). Incompatible `eventProps.type` for an event is warned and skipped (not treated as unfiltered). Valid `custom:*` kebab-case names are registered by the slot runner. UI nodes (including tab **panels**) dispatch locally via `useDispatchAppBuilderCustomEvent` — misses bubble to the parent node, then to the application bus. Root `custom:*` uses `registerAppBuilderCustomActionSlot` scoped by session `namespace` and `dispatchAppBuilderCustomEvent`. Tabs cannot wrap `Tabs.Tab`, so their custom dispatcher wraps panel children instead (not the global bus). Invalid `custom:` names are warned and skipped. Viewport wrap uses `includeCustomEvents={false}` so root `custom:*` is not double-registered. **Registration:** UI pointer/`click`/`contextmenu` via `uiSlotDomProps` on the wrap `Box` (widgets, containers, controls, toolbar items, viewport host). `contextmenu` calls `preventDefault`. Tab controls cannot wrap `Tabs.Tab` (Mantine `Tabs.List` requires it as a direct child), so they put `uiSlotDomProps` on `controlProps` (`ButtonHTMLAttributes`, so new UI events do not need a tab-type edit). Application events register on `AppBuilderPage` via `AppBuilderApplicationActionSlots`: `appready` waits (no timeout) via `waitForAppBuilderViewport` → `viewportAccessFunctions.waitUntilReady`; computation `TASK_START`/`END` for `SESSION_CUSTOMIZATION`; `computationerror` is `TASK_CANCEL` with status `"Session customization failed"` (local session id on the task payload; superseded customizes cancel with a different status); export slots are `TASK_START`/`END`/`CANCEL` for `EXPORT_REQUEST` (`data.sessionId`, `exportId`, `name`, `displayname` — same path as widgets and export parameter value sources). Viewer interaction slot names are `selecton` / `selectoff` / `hoveron` / `hoveroff` (viewer `interaction.multiSelect.*` maps onto the select slots). The ShapeDiver listener enables hover/select like an anchor `selectionProperties` (`useSelection` + passive interaction request, hover default true, min 0 / max 1 / `deselectOnEmpty`, grouped by full effective selection config — conflicting colors/max/hover on the same nameFilter+viewport warn and run as separate groups). After computation it restores selection silently and fires `selecton`/`selectoff` only if the selected name set changed; `processActive` is scoped to this session `namespace`. It runs the matching slot when that viewer event fires on this group's manager. Pair with `setContainerVisibility` to replace `selectionProperties`. ShapeDiver registers `waitUntilReady` from `useViewport` (`waitForViewportScene`: bbox settled with geometry, or empty box when there is none — viewer `calculateZoomTo` no-ops on an empty box). iJewel/WebGi should register its own `waitUntilReady` for host visibility. Hosts without a viewport skip the wait.
- **App Builder contract files:** Action JSON types live in `features/appbuilder/config/appbuilderActions.ts`, action slots in `appbuilderActionSlots.ts`. Parameter value source types stay in `appbuilder.ts` (they are nested in actions and instances, not a separate CrossWindow contract). `appbuilder.ts` re-exports action/slot types. Settings Zod (`appbuilderActionsTypecheck.ts`) and model-state import those files — do not copy the types. CrossWindow `triggerAction` allowlist types stay on `ecommerceapi.ts` (subset of action types, including nested `executeActions`). `triggerAction` `importModelState` is the empty action plus `{modelStateId}` (import without the dialog); the dedicated `importModelState()` method still requires `{modelStateId}`.
- **E-commerce connector / tools API:** Keep two typed CrossWindow facades. Share action cores, not one RPC. Canonical action-prop Zod lives in `features/appbuilder/config/appbuilderActionsTypecheck.ts` (UI-free; includes parameter-source schemas because `setParameterValue.source` and `modelState` sources share createModelState props). Settings JSON (`appbuildertypecheck.ts`) and the e-commerce client (`ecommerceapitypecheck.ts`) import it. Do **not** import `appbuildertypecheck.ts` from the e-commerce client — that module pulls Mantine theme / widget validation. `IAddItemToCartData` is the cart-plugin payload, not addToCart action props. The screenshot tool schema is stricter than `viewportScreenshotPropsSchema`. `getOutput` / `getMetric` share `getOutputContent` (metric maps `content` to `value`). Do **not** put live APIs on `window` (`__appBuilderECommerceConnector` / `__appBuilderToolsApi`). `createECommerceApiConnectorActions` is Zustand-only (no hooks, no agent-tools import); `useECommerceApiConnectorActions` passes `componentContext.actions` so host camera (and other host keys) run through `findAppBuilderActionRegistration`. Playwright drives both APIs from a parent page (`tests/fixtures/cross-window`, `openCrossWindowScenario` / `openToolsApiScenario`) the same way AppBuilderCrossWindowApi does: parent origin `http://127.0.0.1:3000`, App Builder in iframe `name="app"`. E-commerce: parent `ECommerceApiFactory.getConnectorApi`. Tools: settings `agentOverride` (test intercept) so Open agent appears; stub `window.open` to return `window.parent`; parent `ToolsApiFactory.getClientApi(iframe.contentWindow)`. Deployed `appbuilder.shapediver.com` sends `Cross-Origin-Opener-Policy: same-origin`, so a top-level page cannot handshake a localhost popup (`window.opener` is null). Do not add product query params or window hooks for tests. Tools handshake only if an agent window is set; Shopify iframes must not always use `window.parent` (that would spam Tools). `triggerAction` special-cases create/import/reset/undo/redo/addToCart/sound so they skip sharing-URL updates, import dialogs, and toasts (`createModelStateFromStores`, `importModelStateFromStore`, `resetParameterValues(ns, {notify: false})`, `undoParameterHistory` / `redoParameterHistory`, `addToCartFromStores`, `runAppBuilderActionSound`). Remaining types use the action catalog + host overlay. Nested `executeActions` uses the same dispatcher. `setParameterValues` throws on unknown/invalid/missing value-or-source when `strict: true` (e-commerce `triggerAction` and tools camera `run` pass that flag; the connector then returns `{success: false}`). Toolbar / slots / in-app `executeActions` omit `strict` and warn/skip. Tools `runActionControl` camera path uses `AgentToolsDeps.runCameraAction` from `componentContext.actions.camera.run`. `getOutput` / `getMetric` share `getOutputContent`. Screenshot tool output is `image_url`; input is `contentType`, `quality`, `resolution`.
- **Action cores (SS-10025):** Toolbar, action slots, tools `runActionControl`, and e-commerce `triggerAction` share non-React cores. Action-prop Zod: `appbuilderActionsTypecheck.ts` (not copied in ecommerce). Camera: host `componentContext.actions.camera.run` (ShapeDiver registers `runAppBuilderActionCamera` from `AppBuilderRoot.tsx`; named assign is `type: "camera"` + `props.type: "assign"` + `props.props.camera.name`; App Builder `set` requires both position and target; camera action props are a discriminated union on `type`; `camera.type` must be a viewer `CAMERA_TYPE`; missing camera/viewport throws only when `strict: true`). Model state: `createModelStateFromStores` / `importModelStateFromStore` (no sharing-URL update, no toasts). Add to cart: `addToCartFromStores` (no toasts); the toolbar `run` still toasts. Undo/redo/reset: `entities/parameter/lib/undoRedoParameters.ts` and `resetParameterValues(..., {notify: false})`. Output lookup: `getOutputContent` (id/name/displayname). Keep the e-commerce and tools CrossWindow facades separate; do not collapse them into one RPC.
- **Icons:** `IAppBuilderIcon` / `iconType` accept Iconify names, image URLs (http(s), data URI, path; SVG and common rasters), or inline Iconify objects. Detection and `<img>` rendering are centralized in `shared/ui/icon/isIconImageUrl.ts` and `Icon.tsx`. Toolbar buttons must treat URLs as icons (not fallback text).
- **Mobile fallback (SS-10042):** Theme is the general default (`AppBuilderAppShellTemplatePage.defaultProps.mobileFallbacks`, `ViewportAnchor2d/3d.defaultProps.mobileFallback`). JSON overlays defined fields for a single container/anchor; omitted JSON keeps the theme; omitted JSON+theme keeps previous behavior. Applied below AppShell `navbarBreakpoint` (an anchor theme may set `mobileBreakpoint`). `disabled` hides without moving; otherwise content moves. Moves are one hop of original content (incoming extras do not ride along). Merge uses additional-container `position`/`order` (omitted = append).
- **Viewer:** `@shapediver/viewer.*`. `viewer.local.ts` can link `../Viewer`; viewer bugs are fixed there and need a **dev server restart**. Keep `node_modules` in sync (`pnpm install`) when versions differ.

## Git and commits

- Branch names: `task/JIRA-ISSUE-ID`. Every commit message starts with the ticket (`SS-10004: ...`).
- Commits are SSH-signed via 1Password; **signing fails from an agent shell**. Stage and describe; **let the user commit**.
- `git checkout -- <file>` restores from the _index_; use `git checkout HEAD --` when files are staged.

## Line endings and edits

- Working tree is CRLF, git stores LF (`autocrlf`). eslint `linebreak-style: CRLF`.
- **Never** `sed -i` or plain Python writes on source; they produce LF and hundreds of lint errors. Use the Edit tool, or Python with `newline=''` and `\r\n`.

## Checks (judge only files you changed)

```bash
npx prettier --check <files>
npx eslint <files>
npx tsc --noEmit -p .          # root, covers shared
npx jest --config jest.config.mjs src/shared/<path>
```

Some untouched tests have pre-existing prettier violations.

- **Typecheck:** IDE `ReadLints` / ESLint are not a substitute for root `tsc`. After changing `forwardRef` type parameters, host elements (`svg` vs `img`, etc.), or spreading a `ref` onto a third-party component, run `npx tsc --noEmit -p .`. Do not put a union-typed `ref` into a props object that is spread onto a component that only accepts one host type — narrow the ref at each host instead.
- **Mocks:** `jest.mock` replaces **all** exports. When adding a named export that other modules import, search for `jest.mock` of that module and keep named exports via `...jest.requireActual(...)` (override only what the test needs). A passing targeted test is not enough if other suites mock the changed module; run those tests, or `pnpm test` (what CI runs).

## How the user likes to work

- Explain the **root cause** before proposing a fix; then evaluate if a minimal fix makes sense.
- Do **not** deploy or rerun e2e unless asked. Do not edit a file the user is currently editing; propose the change instead.
- After a batch: prettier, eslint, tsc, affected jest, **one** browser verify per fix, then a regression review. Report what was verified and what was not.
- Keep notes on models, coordinates, root causes, and driver pitfalls for later sessions.
- Do not edit `src/` while a browser run is active (HMR reloads the page). One targeted browser run per hypothesis and per fix; no deploy-and-rerun loops unless asked.

## Updating these agent rules

Agents **may edit** files in `.cursor/rules/` or **create new** `.mdc` rules when they learn facts that are not already captured (models, coordinates, root causes, driver pitfalls, store semantics, workflow). Prefer adding to the existing rule that matches the topic (`appbuilder-sdk`, `parameters-and-selection`, `browser-diagnosis`, `e2e-playwright`) over duplicating. Do not invent process the user did not confirm; only record information that was missing.
